```c
static int apply_explicit_mode(const char *path, const parsed_mode_t *pm) {
    struct stat st;
    if (lstat(path, &st) != 0)
        return -1;
    
    mode_t final;
    if (pm->special_preserve) {
        mode_t kernel_special = st.st_mode & 07000;
        mode_t parsed_special = pm->value & 07000;
        final = (kernel_special & ~parsed_special) | pm->value;
    } else {
        final = pm->value & 07777;
    }
    
    return chmod(path, final);
}
```

This handles:
- Numeric ≤4 digits: preserve kernel special bits (e.g., inherited setgid) that aren't in the parsed mode
- Numeric ≥5 digits: apply exactly the specified mode
- Symbolic: apply exactly the computed mode (special bits already correctly determined)

